,{"text":"Net cash of $557.4m against total assets of $832.4m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 27.3% year on year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 38.4% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-258.2% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $5.5m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 21.0% over the year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000162828026049808/0001628280-26-049808-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-049808"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 19.0% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (4,096,866 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1821769/000110465926070115/0001104659-26-070115-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 31.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.31,"consecutive":2,"current":0.387,"current_display":"38.7%","threshold_display":"31.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -42.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.42,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.273,"current_display":"-27.3%","threshold_display":"-42.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":116.131,"current_display":"116 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 28.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.28,"consecutive":1,"current":0.21,"current_display":"21.0%","threshold_display":"28.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"